# Use the image CMD/ENTRYPOINT instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile ENTRYPOINT is a boot wrapper that runs the dind entrypoint
# (which binds the unauthenticated tcp://0.0.0.0:2375 listener) in the
# BACKGROUND and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the exposed Docker API is ALREADY LIVE when the agent starts, making the
#     "edited config but never restarted dockerd" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 stays `sleep infinity`, so restarting dockerd cannot kill the
#     container (the stock foreground `docker-init -- dockerd` would).
#
# dockerd takes ~10s to finish binding; the harness waits SETTLE_SECONDS.
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must RESTART dockerd bound to the unix
# socket only (no tcp 2375), not merely edit a file.
